id: pm-ado-option-contract-1114
title: Adopt pm-cli option contract and current pm-toolchain
description: Supersede Dependabot PR 100 with current published pm-cli and pm-changelog; retain native refusals and unchanged gates.
type: Chore
status: in_progress
priority: 2
tags[2]: dependencies,"gh:unbraind/pm-ado#100"
created_at: "2026-11-14T10:18:01.974Z"
updated_at: "2026-11-14T14:55:30.654Z"
author: codex-toolchain-1114a
comments[3]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-11-14T10:18:49.852Z",codex-toolchain-1114a,"Initial failures reproduced against pm-cli 2026.11.14. GH-1665 (CHANGELOG 2026.11.8) normalizes direct option spellings, defaults and coercion through the CLI path; numeric project/type/items fixtures no longer prove handler type refusals. Replace these with repeated scalar arrays reachable through actual CLI flags, retain fingerprint and configuration refusals, and assert no authoritative writes. The npm package omits CHANGELOG.md from its files allowlist; reviewed the upstream changelog instead. Current pins: pm-cli 2026.11.14 and pm-changelog 2026.11.13."
  "2026-11-14T10:21:15.433Z",codex-toolchain-1114a,"Failure -> cause -> fix: contracts handler numeric project/type -> GH-1665 CLI string coercion -> empty project and dot type selections plus malformed fingerprint strings, with native CLI code 2 and no-write proof; move handler numeric items and boolean fingerprint -> GH-1665 coercion -> empty items selection code 2 and bad fingerprint schema_changed code 4, retaining missing options and blank type configuration code 2. Native repeated scalar flags retain their last value, so arrays were rejected as replacement fixtures. No production source changed: existing exported raw command-context validators still protect direct callers; real CLI semantic validation remains reachable. Original focused files failed 2 of 47 tests on the new pin; the unchanged old assertions provide migration revert proof. Full coverage/release matrices are delegated to CI because the existing full consumer run already exceeded 15 minutes before its repeated coverage pass; local focused, compile and docstring checks remain required."
  "2026-11-14T14:55:30.654Z",codex-toolchain-1114a,"Failure | Cause (host contract) | Fix\n--- | --- | ---\nhandler validates configuration, maps and schema pins with typed shell exits | GH-1665: declared string options now use CLI coercion before dispatch. | Replace numeric project/type cases with empty project and dot type strings; retain typed configuration exit 2 and authoritative no-write snapshots.\nhost refuses malformed options, missing binding/credentials, schema drift and failed SDK reads | GH-1665: CLI-spelled keys are honored and raw values become CLI strings. | Retain empty selection refusal and malformed fingerprint strings with their selection/schema-change codes, exit statuses and no-write checks.\n\nContract reference: [pm-cli 2026.11.8 migration entries](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-cli/blob/main/CHANGELOG.md#2026118---2026-11-08). Full gate results and timing limits are recorded in the preceding validation receipts. No workload or coverage threshold was lowered. This final comment makes the failure/cause/fix mapping explicit; source files are unchanged."
files[4]{path,scope}:
  package-lock.json,project
